Package: mlmr
Title: A Guided Interface for Mixed-Effects and Multilevel Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Marcus", "Harris", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "marcus.harris.uconn@gmail.com")
Description: Provides a guided Shiny interface and reusable R helpers for
    specifying, fitting, explaining, and reporting mixed-effects and multilevel
    models with 'lme4' (Bates, Maechler, Bolker, and Walker, 2015,
    <doi:10.18637/jss.v067.i01>). The package supports grand-mean and
    cluster-mean centering (Enders and Tofighi, 2007,
    <doi:10.1037/1082-989X.12.2.121>), nested, longitudinal, and crossed
    random-effects structures, interaction terms, optional Satterthwaite and
    Kenward-Roger denominator degrees of freedom via 'lmerTest' (Kuznetsova,
    Brockhoff, and Christensen, 2017, <doi:10.18637/jss.v082.i13>), marginal
    and conditional R-squared (Nakagawa, Johnson, and Schielzeth, 2017,
    <doi:10.1098/rsif.2017.0213>), random-intercept reliability, level-by-level
    and combined equations, APA-style tables, diagnostics, reproducible R code,
    and publication archive bundles.
